module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a construction that accepts a body of unestablished shape reaches a serializer that walks only some of that body's positional children, so admitted siblings vanish from the emitted program with no refusal. HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5) -- the emit is plausible partial output, not a located diagnostic, and a later consumer runs a different program than the one authored.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-11, srv1 workspace bring-up findings ledger F37 (bash subshell drops the right operand), ledger v3 numbering, operator review of source pinned to main at acc218340ed6e24a9ad06c550a5494307d0320bb (a source review that did not rerun srv1). bash_build_subshell accepts any Node body. The shared bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list (v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize) reads positional children 0 and 1 only, so an or_else node passed as the body keeps left and drops right, with no refusal arm (v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build). Two insufficient boundaries: the body carrier does not establish grammar membership, and the serializer turns an unestablished shape into plausible partial output. The incident's caller fix (bash_build_subshell_from_stmts) leaves the shared reader able to drop behavior through other consumers. Durable repair: establish shape at construction, preserve every admitted child, refuse malformed input. No new Bash representation. Roadmap leaf cc-structural-carriers.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is not a missing flatten of a well-formed cons list -- a two-child cons is the shape the walker implements. It is not a target-language defect: the same Node is admitted at construction. The class is the pair: an untyped body formal plus a walker that silently truncates. RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent drop. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- malformed bodies are authorable and the admitted-child set is decidable from the Node tree.",

    "CLIMBED, 2026-10-13, gentle-koi-908. bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list now returns Outcome and refuses a body that is not the untagged cons encoding (extra positional child, production Atom at child 0, or empty children), located at the body node with reason bash_fold_serialize_stmt_list_malformed. Shared consumers: subshell, if, if-else statement-list bodies, and the word-list spelling helper that reused the same walker. Constructors still accept any Node (no new Bash representation); the wall is the serialize path that renders deploy and apply scripts (bash_fold_serialize_node / bash_emit_stmts). Discriminating RED: or_else or a command as a subshell or if body refuses typed and located. Positive control: or_else as a statement inside a well-formed list keeps both sides. AUDIT of bash_build constructors: subshell, if, and if-else were the flatten consumers and are covered by the shared refuse. bash_build_word_cmdsubst serializes its body as a single statement via bash_fold_serialize_node, so an or_else body is preserved rather than truncated; a statement-list body is an unsupported production, not a silent drop. Remaining tagged builders (command, assign, exit, and_then, or_else, pipe, redir, negation) are statements, not statement-list walkers. RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed on the emit path (DESIGN 4b rung 3) -- the source can still construct a malformed body Node, but no Accepted serialize contains a truncated emit. NEXT TRIGGER: construction itself inhabits a statement-list carrier so a malformed body is unwritable (structurally impossible) rather than refused at serialize.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize", decl_name: "bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.bash_command_fold", decl_name: "bash_fold_subshell_or_else_body_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.bash_command_fold", decl_name: "bash_fold_subshell_or_else_as_stmt_preserves_both_sides_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
